{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The receiver matches readiness to the exact returned context; it does not remap a later context to earlier requests. The leader’s confirmation queue can release several requests together, but its forwarded replies use the latest confirmation’s context for all of them. I’ll retain this as a correlation question, with client timeout behavior and any wider progress consequence still separate.\n"}}
